<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chak Tok Ich'aak I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 378</span> · Also known as Great Jaguar Paw</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chak Tok Ich'aak I was a king of the Maya city of Tikal in the fourth century CE. Inscriptions record that he died on the same day in January 378 that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siyaj-kak">Siyaj K'ak'</a>, a warrior linked to Teotihuacan, arrived at Tikal, an event widely interpreted as a Teotihuacan-backed intervention or conquest. He was followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yax-nuun-ayiin-i">Yax Nuun Ayiin I</a>, a new ruler with Teotihuacan connections.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chak-tok-ichaak-i.jpg" alt="Chak Tok Ich'aak I" width="320" height="691" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HJPD · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tikal_St26.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
